Z||000002||mbramble||01-05-2001||10:03 AM||||If you are interested in installing stock Fiero aero (GT) trim, you can check the Mall, e-bay, or you can do a Yahoo search for on-line Fiero club links.  Most of them have 'classifieds' where members are selling Fiero stuff.  <P>You need an aero front and rear fascia and the ground f/x pieces (for front fenders, doors, rear 1/4 fenders, and the aero rocker panels and whatever hardware is necessary to mount them all).  You may also have to change your trim moulding to match what comes on the aero fascias and will need new side marker lights.<P>I currently have an aero nose on my Coupe and the rest is stock.  I would like to get the rest of the f/x pieces (I have them for the doors) but it is too cold to think about working on such things right now!!<P>Here's a link to before and after pictures of my coupe's 'nose job'.  <A HREF="http://www.bramblett.com/fiero/bef-aft.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.bramblett.com/fiero/bef-aft.jpg</A> <p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 01-05-2001).]||||reg||1
